# Final self-check before answering

Confirm every point; if any fails, fix the proposal rather than emitting it.

- Output is one JSON object: an `epics` array and `planner_notes`, nothing else.
- No tickets, no dependencies — those are later stages.
- You did NOT number your epics: no `new_epic:<n>` appears in your output; the
  environment assigns those indices by your emission order.
- No invented epic keys; new epics use `"key": null`; existing epics echo their
  exact key.
- Every `source_anchor` is one of the Valid source anchors, copied verbatim —
  none constructed, slugified, or guessed.
- Output is schema-valid with no surrounding text.
